{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/26887-changeling-deck-of-cards","id":26887,"title":"Changeling deck of cards","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-09T18:39:00-08:00","id":26887,"title":"Changeling deck of cards","content":"When CtD first came out in 1995, the first edition made use of a deck of cards in play. This was generally considered to be a Bad Move, as the deck of cards had to be purchased separately and often wasn\u2019t available from the same souce that sold the book. In 1996 when the second edition came out, the Changeling cards system was dropped like a hot potato, and rightfully so.<br /> <br /> But now we\u2019re in 2013, with Print-on-Demand technology and digital publishing. I still thnk it would be a bad idea fo a game to <i>demand</i> the use of a customized deck of cards the way that Changeling did; but a number of game systems are providing custom decks as a game aid: Fate Core has the Deck of Fate which can replace its custom dice, act as Fate Points, and give ideas for Aspects; God-Machine Chronicle just released a deck of Condition Cards, something which I suspect will become standard practice for all of the post-GMC nWoD gamelines.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m thinking that it might be interesting if and when they publish a 20th Anniversary Edition for Changeling: the Dreaming for them to bring back the Bunk deck as an optional system in the game. This would ideally be the same deck that was designed for use with the first edition, although perhaps a redesign aimed at giving th cards a more diverse set of uses would be in order.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T19:01:20-08:00","id":26901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/26887-changeling-deck-of-cards#post26887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m thinking that it might be interesting if and when they publish a 20th Anniversary Edition for Changeling: the Dreaming for them to bring back the Bunk deck as an optional system in the game. This would <b>ideally be the same deck</b> that was designed for use with the first edition, although perhaps a redesign aimed at giving th cards a more diverse set of uses would be in order.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not going to happen unfortunately, since the original files for that deck are unrecoverable.<br /> <br /> Now, a new deck with new art designed for the new print methods could be very cool.<br /> <br /> -MMM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T19:07:40-08:00","id":26908,"title":"","content":"I don't think I'd like to see the cantrip card system come back as mandatory. My players and I enjoy the more free form bunk system. That being said, I think a cantrip card stretch goal for a hypothetical Changeling 20 Kickstarter would be awesome! I could see it being an optional cantrip card rule sheet PDF along with a set of print and play/PoD cards. The deck rules would need to be revised and clarified from what appeared in 1st edition. The art and realm cards would also need to be revised significantly. A lot of them changed in 2nd. Hopefully, they'll be changed a bit more if there's a C20. The card layout would also need to change to fit DriveThru's format. I'd like to see some of the art reused. Those cards were beautiful, and I don't think many current players have had a chance to see them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T19:26:38-08:00","id":26918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/26887-changeling-deck-of-cards?p=26908#post26908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I'd like to see the cantrip card system come back as mandatory. My players and I enjoy the more free form bunk system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/26887-changeling-deck-of-cards?p=26908#post26908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, I think a cantrip card stretch goal for a hypothetical Changeling 20 Kickstarter would be awesome! I could see it being an optional cantrip card rule sheet PDF along with a set of print and play/PoD cards. The deck rules would need to be revised and clarified from what appeared in 1st edition. The art and realm cards would also need to be revised significantly. A lot of them changed in 2nd. Hopefully, they'll be changed a bit more if there's a C20. The card layout would also need to change to fit DriveThru's format. I'd like to see some of the art reused. Those cards were beautiful, and I don't think many current players have had a chance to see them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve barely gotten a glimpse of them, myself. Yes, I thnk this would be a wonderful Stretch Goal for said Kickstarter. Mind you, the rules for using said cards would probably have to be included with the deck; but that strikes me as a pretty good option anyway: those who aren\u2019t interested in the deck could completely ignore it, while those who like it would have everything they need for it in one place. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s too bad that the original artwork is unrecoverable. But it\u2019s more the homage to the original concept that I was thinking of; so new artwork in the spirit of the original artwork ought to be fine. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T02:02:14-08:00","id":27066,"title":"","content":"I do remember those cards. I can't remember if I collected enough to have a full deck of them or not.<br /> <br /> Maybe the cards can be re-released in a PDF print format the same way Fan Made Rage decks are distributed. I have to agree that I would not like to see them made mandatory or even replace dice use. However I would like to see them as a bonus collection to add to your game the same way you can buy a Wild West Poker deck and Mage Tarot deck. I do really like the artwork. I wish that they could be used with more recent versions of Changeling, but for that to work the cards and maybe even Changeling's magic system itself needs a lot of work that never got ironed out in a Revised edition. By that time they wouldn't even resemble the original cantrip cards probably. Maybe Stephani Pui-Mun Law can contribute the way she did for the Mage Awakening Tarot. She does such great artwork with such ephemeral and fantastical themes. She's got a website here: <a href=\"http://www.shadowscapes.com/main.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.shadowscapes.com/main.php</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T12:42:56-08:00","id":27408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe the cards can be re-released in a PDF print format the same way Fan Made Rage decks are distributed. </div> </div> </div>I do artwork for the Fan-made Rage sets. And all the art is either volunteer work from Rage fans, finished artwork where we ask permission to use, or sometimes commissioned from artists that the play testers like. There was at least one artist who had finished artwork (From DA) who much later decided they no longer wanted their artwork used anymore, so Fenris had to replace that artwork. I do think you are referring to the Least Wanted Set, though, right?<br /> Also Drivethrucards.com does give you PDF print format to print cards from.<br /> <br /> My take is that the only way to replace the old unworkable art files for the Bunk cards is to get physical copies of the cards themselves and scan them. And good luck with that! Last time I saw a box or full collection of cards on ebay, they were going for $200-and above. About as bad as trying to get a Booster Box of War of the Amazon.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Stephani Pui-Mun Law! I remember that I bought a print from her way back at one of the Anime Expo conventions I went to! I think I still have it. It was &quot;Cat Knot&quot; with the winged Siamese cat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 12-10-2013, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T12:59:08-08:00","id":27434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt-M-McElroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/26887-changeling-deck-of-cards?p=26901#post26901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not going to happen unfortunately, since the original files for that deck are unrecoverable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sad to hear that the old files are corrupted. If scans are ever needed of the original cantrip cards, I have a complete set of them and am happy to scan them!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T02:21:01-08:00","id":27848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/26887-changeling-deck-of-cards?p=27434#post27434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sad to hear that the old files are corrupted. If scans are ever needed of the original cantrip cards, I have a complete set of them and am happy to scan them!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm getting the impression that might not be acceptable or legal from someone not in the company even if it was given back to the company. That said I'm sure plenty of fans would send their cards back to onyx Path just so they have the artwork again. I think it's also a matter of scale. The scans, even with a high DPI would not be the same quality as the originals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T06:20:50-08:00","id":27933,"title":"","content":"Just throwing it out there for the folks at Onyx Path and OneBookShelf.<br /> <br /> You're right that they wouldn't be the same quality as the originals, but with a good enough scan it could be acceptable. A few of the PoD books are done from scans since the original files aren't usable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T14:29:08-08:00","id":28304,"title":"","content":"Yes. C20 Edition and new and old Cantrip Cards as Strech Goal. That would be relly great and I would throw my money at Onyx Path...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>27 Years of Roleplay and almost sane...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/183-assassin","name":"Assassin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar183_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T18:23:06-08:00","id":785666,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the necro, but with C20 on the horizon, now seems as good a time as any to add my support for an optional set of cantrip cards.<br /> <br /> If the scanned originals won't provide decent files (it depends on the scanner, the cards and the lamination), the other option is to hand over the original set to the original artist(s) and get them to recreate the artwork. It might just be simpler to create new art, though. Either way, I'm happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}